<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port Dos Bocas reopens as winds ebb.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port Dos Bocas reopens as winds ebb.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico crude port Dos Bocas in Tabasco state reopened as of 5:30 p.m. (2330 GMT) to larger ships, according to port captain Jorge Rojano Rodriguez.</p>
<p>The port had been shut since 5:30 p.m. Sunday because of winds of 25 to 35 kilometers per hour, he said.</p>
<p>Resumption of crude oil tanker shipping would be delayed until Tuesday, as the ships do not leave port after dark, Rojano said.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
